### Orvexa API v1 — journey step 02: customer identity
### Create a customer with channel identifiers, resolve an identifier back to
### the same customer (normalization: phone → E.164 digits, email lowercase),
### list + get. The tenant derives from the API key — never from the body.

@ORVEXA_URL = {{$processEnv ORVEXA_URL}}
@ORVEXA_KEY = {{$processEnv ORVEXA_KEY}}

### Create a customer with two channel identities → 201
# @name createCustomer
POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/customers
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "display_name": "Jane Wanjiku",
  "language": "en",
  "timezone": "Africa/Nairobi",
  "identifiers": [
    { "type": "phone", "value": "+254 712 345 678" },
    { "type": "whatsapp", "value": "+254712345678", "is_primary": true }
  ],
  "tags": ["pilot"]
}

###

### Resolve by the normalized phone digits → 200, same customer id
# (254712345678 == +254712345678 == +254 712 345 678 — one identity, no forks)
# @name resolvePhone
POST {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/customers/resolve
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "phone",
  "value": "254712345678"
}

###

### List customers (cursor pagination; limit ≤ 100)
# @name listCustomers
GET {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/customers?limit=25
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}

###

### Get the customer created above
# @name getCustomer
GET {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/customers/{{createCustomer.response.body.$.data.id}}
X-API-Key: {{ORVEXA_KEY}}
